    <h2>4. The Shared Responsibility Model</h2>
    <p class="lead">The most misunderstood concept in cloud security — and the one that leads to most security failures — is the Shared Responsibility Model. This model defines precisely who is responsible for what in a cloud environment: the cloud provider, and you (the customer).</p>

    <div class="analogy">
      <div class="analogy-label">Analogy — The Apartment Building</div>
      <p>Imagine renting an apartment. The <strong>landlord</strong> is responsible for the building's structure, plumbing, electrical wiring, and roof. <strong>You</strong> are responsible for locking your door, not leaving valuables in plain sight, and managing who has a key. If the building's elevator breaks, that's on the landlord. If you leave your apartment unlocked and get robbed, that's on you. The cloud works exactly the same way.</p>
